IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part2`
IMPORT `ea-part2-continuity`
IMPORT `ea-part3-salary`
IMPORT `ea-part4-hours`
IMPORT `ea-part9-maternity`
IMPORT `ea-part10-leave`
IMPORT `ea-part12-records`
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`
IMPORT `ea-retrenchment-reporting-notification`
IMPORT `ea-seat`

-- Employment Act 1968 -- the seat layer, worked cases.
--
-- SEAT: the employee. Every fixture and every expected value below is copied
-- from the existing case files (ea-part2-cases.l4, ea-parts-3-and-4-cases.l4,
-- ea-parts-5-to-12-cases.l4, ea-retrenchment-reporting-notification-cases.l4),
-- where they were hand-checked. Nothing is computed afresh here.

§ `Fixtures, copied from the existing case files`

GIVEN `w26` IS A BOOLEAN, `y2` IS A BOOLEAN, `y5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ServiceLength
DECIDE `service` `w26` `y2` `y5` IS
    ServiceLength WITH
        `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `w26`
        `employed for 2 years or more` IS `y2`
        `employed for 5 years or more` IS `y5`

`a new starter` MEANS `service` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ten years in` MEANS `service` TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN `provides` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER, `symmetrical` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ContractTerms
DECIDE `terms` `provides` `days` `symmetrical` IS
    ContractTerms WITH
        `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `provides`
        `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `days`
        `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS `symmetrical`

`a silent contract` MEANS `terms` FALSE 0 TRUE
`a generous contract of 60 days` MEANS `terms` TRUE 60 TRUE
`a mean contract of 1 day` MEANS `terms` TRUE 1 TRUE

GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER, `leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Absence
DECIDE `an absence of` `days` `leave` `excuse` `informed` IS
    Absence WITH
        `days absent continuously` IS `days`
        `with prior leave from the employer` IS `leave`
        `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS `excuse`
        `the employee informed or attempted to inform the employer of the excuse` IS `informed`

GIVEN `immediate` IS A BOOLEAN, `undertook the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DangerFacts
DECIDE `danger that is` `immediate` `undertook the risk` IS
    DangerFacts WITH
        `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant` IS TRUE
        `the danger is immediate` IS `immediate`
        `the danger is to the person` IS TRUE
        `the danger is by violence or disease` IS TRUE
        `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk` IS `undertook the risk`

GIVEN `misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DismissalFacts
DECIDE `dismissal facts` `misconduct` `inquiry` `suspended` `days` IS
    DismissalFacts WITH
        `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS `misconduct`
        `the employer held a due inquiry` IS `inquiry`
        `the employee was instead down-graded` IS FALSE
        `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS `suspended`
        `the days of suspension` IS `days`

GIVEN `manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `with notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `in lieu` IS A BOOLEAN, `six months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Dismissed
DECIDE `a dismissed employee` `manager` `with notice` `in lieu` `six months` IS
    Dismissed WITH
        `in a managerial or an executive position` IS `manager`
        `dismissed with notice` IS `with notice`
        `dismissed without notice but paid salary in lieu` IS `in lieu`
        `served that employer for at least 6 months in any position` IS `six months`

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER, `redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN, `ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ServiceForBenefits
DECIDE `service for benefits` `years` `redundancy` `ceased` IS
    ServiceForBenefits WITH
        `years of continuous service with the employer` IS `years`
        `dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation` IS `redundancy`
        `the service has ceased` IS `ceased`

`consent given and standing` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS TRUE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS FALSE
`consent given then withdrawn` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS TRUE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS TRUE
`no consent` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS FALSE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS FALSE

GIVEN `proposed` IS A NUMBER, `loss` IS A NUMBER, `permitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `showed cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DamagesDeduction
DECIDE `a damages deduction` `proposed` `loss` `permitted` `showed cause` IS
    DamagesDeduction WITH
        `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default` IS `loss`
        `one month's wages` IS 2000
        `the amount the employer proposes to deduct` IS `proposed`
        `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS `permitted`
        `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS `showed cause`

GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `own request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RestDayWork
DECIDE `rest day work` `hours` `own request` IS
    RestDayWork WITH
        `hours agreed as the usual hours of work per day were agreed` IS FALSE
        `the agreed usual hours of work per day` IS 0
        `the hours actually worked on the rest day` IS `hours`
        `the basic rate of pay for one day's work` IS 100
        `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 12.5
        `the work was at the employee's own request` IS `own request`

GIVEN `months total` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER, `months in year` IS A NUMBER, `absent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LeaveService
DECIDE `leave service` `months total` `years` `months in year` `absent` IS
    LeaveService WITH
        `completed months of service with the employer` IS `months total`
        `completed 12 month periods of continuous service` IS `years`
        `completed months of service in that year` IS `months in year`
        `absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` IS `absent`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER, `examined` IS A BOOLEAN, `hospital` IS A BOOLEAN, `hosp days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A SickLeaveFacts
DECIDE `sick facts` `months` `examined` `hospital` `hosp days` IS
    SickLeaveFacts WITH
        `completed months of service with the employer` IS `months`
        `examined by a medical practitioner` IS `examined`
        `hospitalisation is necessary` IS `hospital`
        `days on which the employee is hospitalised` IS `hosp days`

GIVEN `arrangement` IS AN AbsenceArrangement, `current` IS A BOOLEAN, `months` IS A NUMBER
    , `daily` IS A NUMBER, `worked days` IS A NUMBER, `other employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MaternityFacts
DECIDE `maternity facts` `arrangement` `current` `months` `daily` `worked days` `other employer` IS
    MaternityFacts WITH
        `the arrangement` IS `arrangement`
        `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS `current`
        `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS `months`
        `the gross rate of pay for one day` IS `daily`
        `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS `worked days`
        `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS `other employer`

GIVEN `after 2016` IS A BOOLEAN, `min period` IS A BOOLEAN, `given` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A KeyTermsFacts
DECIDE `key terms` `after 2016` `min period` `given` `days` IS
    KeyTermsFacts WITH
        `the contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016` IS `after 2016`
        `employed for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS `min period`
        `a written record of the key employment terms was given` IS `given`
        `days after the start of employment when it was given` IS `days`
        `another period has been prescribed in substitution` IS FALSE
        `the substituted period in days` IS 0

GIVEN `under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `end date` IS A BOOLEAN, `months` IS A NUMBER
    , `workforce` IS A NUMBER
    , `employer's initiative` IS A BOOLEAN, `redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `given on` IS A NUMBER, `takes effect on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice of retrenchment`
DECIDE `a notice` `under the Act` `end date` `months` `workforce` `employer's initiative` `redundancy` `given on` `takes effect on` IS
    `Notice of retrenchment` WITH
        `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act` IS `under the Act`
        `the contract` IS `Contract of service` WITH
            `specifies an end date` IS `end date`
            `term of employment in months` IS `months`
        `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS `workforce`
        `the employer initiated the termination` IS `employer's initiative`
        `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation` IS `redundancy`
        `the day the notice is given` IS `given on`
        `the day the notice takes effect` IS `takes effect on`

§ `Notice, and leaving the job`

-- The contract's 1 day is void for a ten-year employee: 28 days. Lawful for a
-- new starter: 1 day. A generous 60 days stands.
#ASSERT `How many days of notice am I owed` `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `How many days of notice am I owed` `a mean contract of 1 day` `a new starter` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How many days of notice am I owed` `a generous contract of 60 days` `ten years in` EQUALS 60

#ASSERT `How much must I be paid in lieu of notice` 200 `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 5600
#ASSERT `How much must I be paid in lieu of notice` 200 `a silent contract` `a new starter` EQUALS 200

#ASSERT NOT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` (`an absence of` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` (`an absence of` 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` (`an absence of` 10 FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` (`an absence of` 10 FALSE TRUE FALSE)

#ASSERT `May I leave without notice because of danger` (`danger that is` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `May I leave without notice because of danger` (`danger that is` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `May I leave without notice because of danger` (`danger that is` TRUE TRUE)

§ `Dismissal and suspension`

#ASSERT `Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` (`dismissal facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)

#ASSERT `Is my suspension without pay lawful` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE 7)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my suspension without pay lawful` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE 8)

#ASSERT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`a dismissed employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`a dismissed employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`a dismissed employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`a dismissed employee` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `Am I barred from a retrenchment benefit by my short service` (`service for benefits` 1.5 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I barred from a retrenchment benefit by my short service` (`service for benefits` 2 TRUE TRUE)

§ `Being paid`

#ASSERT `Was I paid late` `dismissal by the employer` 4
#ASSERT NOT `Was I paid late` `dismissal by the employer` 3
#ASSERT NOT `Was I paid late` `termination by the employee without notice` 7

#ASSERT `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `absence from work` `no consent`
#ASSERT `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `consent given and standing`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `consent given then withdrawn`

#ASSERT `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` (`a damages deduction` 400 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` (`a damages deduction` 600 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` (`a damages deduction` 10 900 FALSE FALSE) `the proportions as the Act states them`

§ `Hours, rest days and overtime`

#ASSERT `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` (Worker WITH `is a workman` IS TRUE, `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS FALSE, `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS 4500) `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` (Worker WITH `is a workman` IS TRUE, `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS FALSE, `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS 4501) `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` (Worker WITH `is a workman` IS FALSE, `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS TRUE, `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS 1000) `the caps as the Act states them`

#ASSERT `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` (`rest day work` 4 TRUE) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` (`rest day work` 10 TRUE) EQUALS 137.5
#ASSERT `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` (`rest day work` 10 FALSE) EQUALS 237.5

#ASSERT `What is my overtime pay` 2 12.5 EQUALS 37.5

